# starformation_and_feedback with R3's flags (FIREmodeOn 0, the FIREmodeOn 0 twin of the R3 fixture of the same rows), SFprescription 1,
# BulgeSizeOn 3) at substep 0 for the satellite of a real R3 FoF group at Snap_63; a stable
# disk after star formation.
# End-of-snapshot output values used as plausible call inputs, not reconstructed call-time
# state (the writer stores these fields verbatim; DiskScaleRadius is the output's DiskRadius;
# MassLoading is the stale value SAGE26 left, which the FIRE path overwrites). Constructed:
# OutflowRate 0 (its value at substep 0 after the first-occupied reset,
# R/src/core_build_model.c:276) and zero histories, as at substep 0; the timing is the c05 R0
# templates' (c03's Age values). Each galaxy's stored SnapNum is the output snapshot, as
# during the next snapshot's evolution, and ZZ[SnapNum] is SAGE26's 1/AA - 1.
# galaxy 0: R3 reference /Volumes/Internal/results/sage26-campaign/workspace/e01-reference/out/R3/model_0.hdf5 (SHA-256 ab278992616f7137b526e5bd3a43045f2e753e29d84997fc69350255c38f570c), Snap_63 row 0 (GalaxyIndex 0, Type 0)
# galaxy 1: R3 reference /Volumes/Internal/results/sage26-campaign/workspace/e01-reference/out/R3/model_0.hdf5 (SHA-256 ab278992616f7137b526e5bd3a43045f2e753e29d84997fc69350255c38f570c), Snap_63 row 3 (GalaxyIndex 252, Type 1)
# Reachability: R3-reachable
format sage26-oracle-fixture 1
routine starformation_and_feedback_fire

